  "correct": "4",
  "solution": "Given:\n\n(a + b) : (b + c) : (c + a) = 15 : 14 : 11\n\na + b + c = 40\n\nCalculation:\n\nLet the common ratio be P.\n\n(a + b) = 15P ....(1)\n\n(b + c) = 14P ....(2)\n\n(c + a) = 11P ....(3)\n\n(1) + (2) + (3),\n\n2(a + b + c) = 40P\n\n⇒ (a + b + c) = 20P\n\n⇒ 40 = 20P\n\n⇒ P = 2\n\nHence,\n\n(a + b) = 30 ....(1)\n\n(b + c) = 28 ....(2)\n\n(c + a) = 22 ....(3)\n\n(a + b + c) = 40 ....(4)\n\nUsing four of the equations,\n\na = 12\n\nb = 18\n\nc = 10\n\nSo, (3a + b - 4c) = 36 + 18 - 40 = 14\n\n**∴ 14 is the required value (3a + b - 4c).**",
